From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:29:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] project: lk2nd-msm8996: Allow 70 MiB for the kernel and
 ramdisk

The Galaxy Tab S3 kernels are 34.5 MiB with BSS and the postmarketOS
initramfs is 13 MiB, which doesn't fit the 50 MiB default together with
the 2 MiB for the device tree. Mainline device trees reserve nothing
below 0x84700000 on this tablet, and lk2nd maps 88 MiB from the start of
DDR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
---
 project/lk2nd-msm8996.mk | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/project/lk2nd-msm8996.mk b/project/lk2nd-msm8996.mk
index db22b6a66..1034b461b 100644
--- a/project/lk2nd-msm8996.mk
+++ b/project/lk2nd-msm8996.mk
@@ -1,3 +1,10 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
 TARGET := msm8996
+
+# Kernels with most drivers built in are larger than the default 50 MiB allows
+# with an initramfs next to them. Mainline device trees reserve nothing below
+# 0x84700000 (Samsung debug buffers on the Galaxy Tab S3), and lk2nd maps 88 MiB
+# from the start of DDR.
+LK2ND_BOOT_MEM_SIZE := 0x04600000
+
 include lk2nd/project/lk2nd.mk
